@* The outer preview document: toolbar, and a width-constrained frame holding the page itself.

   It carries no @@rendermode, no blazor.web.js and no ImportMap, exactly like the delivery document
   it wraps — the device buttons are links and the toolbar is static markup, so there is nothing here
   that needs a circuit. Serving the backoffice shell would download the editor into a frame whose
   only job is to show what a reader would see. *@
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>Preview — @Chrome.Version.Title</title>
    @* Belt and braces with the X-Robots-Tag header the endpoint sets: the header covers the
       response, this covers a copy somebody saves or a crawler that only reads markup. *@
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/site.css" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/preview.css" />
</head>
<body class="cms-preview">
<PreviewToolbar Chrome="Chrome" />
<div class="@Chrome.ViewportCssClass">
    <iframe class="cms-preview-frame" src="@Chrome.ContentUrl" title="Page preview"></iframe>
</div>
</body>
</html>
